{"Title":"An Act authorizing the transfer of real property from the Silver Lake regional school district to the town of Kingston","BillNumber":"S3008","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2024-12-26T11:16:29.873"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2024-12-26T11:16:29.8733333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S3008/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, December 26, 2024 -- Text of the Senate amendment (Senator Lovely) to the House Bill relative to the transfer of real property from the Silver Lake regional school district to the town of Kingston (House, No. 4874). ","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding any general or special law to the contrary, the Silver Lake regional school district may transfer to the town of Kingston ownership of the parcel consisting of 0.19 acres on Lake street in the town of Kingston as shown on the town of Kingston assessors’ map number 8, block 40.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}